{"command": "sed -n 60,116p /testbed/specs/001-transactions/spec.md; echo ===HANDOFF===; cat /testbed/HANDOFF.md", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "2. **Given** a cache with maxsize 2 holding k1 (oldest) and k2, **When** put(k3) is called, **Then** k1 is evicted, len(cache) is 2, and get(k1) raises KeyError.\n3. **Given** a live entry k, **When** put(k, value, tags=(\"a\", 1)) is attempted (invalid tag), **Then** ValueError is raised and k retains its old value, old tags, and its prior recency position (a subsequent eviction evicts the least-recently-used entry, not k, if k was not the LRU).\n\n### Edge Cases\n\n- Empty tag iterable (default) - entry stored with no tags; cannot be removed by any invalidate(tag).\n- Duplicate tags in one put - deduplicated; membership counted once.\n- invalidate(tag) with a tag never used - returns 0, no error.\n- put with the same key and same value but different tags - old tag memberships replaced by new ones.\n- Eviction of an entry, then re-put of the same key - no stale tag membership from the evicted incarnation remains.\n- get on an entry refreshes its recency, protecting it from being the next eviction.\n- Unhashable keys - rejected with the standard unhashable-key error, state unchanged.\n- maxsize of 1 - every put evicts the previous entry (after recency refresh on overwrite, the overwritten key survives its own overwrite).\n\n## Requirements *(mandatory)*\n\n### Functional Requirements\n\n- **FR-001**: The feature MUST expose a new bounded tagged cache construct, TaggedCache, created with a single maxsize argument, in addition to (never replacing) all existing cachetools public APIs, which MUST remain behaviorally unchanged.\n- **FR-002**: put(key, value, tags=()) MUST insert a new entry or replace an existing one for the same key; keys MUST be hashable and unhashable keys MUST be rejected without state change.\n- **FR-003**: get(key) MUST return a detached deep copy of the stored value and MUST raise KeyError for missing keys; values MUST be deep-copied on input to put so that later mutation of the caller's original object never affects the cache.\n- **FR-004**: tags MUST be a finite iterable of strings; tags MUST be deduplicated; a bare string passed as tags and any non-string entry within the iterable MUST be rejected with ValueError before any existing state is changed.\n- **FR-005**: invalidate(tag) MUST remove exactly the currently cached entries carrying that tag and MUST return the number of entries removed; entries without the tag MUST survive; an unused tag MUST yield 0.\n- **FR-006**: Replacing an existing key via put MUST remove the entry's previous tag memberships, so only the new tags apply afterwards.\n- **FR-007**: LRU eviction MUST remove the least-recently-used live entry and MUST NOT leave stale tag memberships that affect later reuse of the same key or invalidate() counts.\n- **FR-008**: get(key) on a present key MUST refresh that entry's LRU recency, making it the most-recently-used entry.\n- **FR-009**: Overwriting an existing key via put MUST refresh that entry's LRU recency, making it the most-recently-used entry (Claim-A extension, variant put_no_recency_refresh, dated 2026-09-21; see Assumptions for the variant-name ambiguity).\n- **FR-010**: len(cache) MUST count only live (currently cached) entries at all times.\n- **FR-011**: maxsize MUST be a positive integer; booleans MUST be excluded even though they are integers; zero, negative, and non-integer values MUST be rejected at construction.\n- **FR-012**: An invalid replacement (e.g. put with invalid tags on an existing key) MUST leave the old value, old tags, and the entry's recency position unchanged.\n- **FR-013**: Every stored value MUST cost exactly one capacity slot regardless of the object's size or complexity.\n\n### Key Entities\n\n- **Cache Entry**: One key-value pair occupying a single capacity slot; attributes: key (hashable), value (stored as a deep copy), tag set (deduplicated strings), recency position (most- to least-recently-used).\n- **Tag**: A string label shared across entries; defines invalidation groups; has no state of its own beyond the set of live entries currently carrying it.\n- **Cache**: The bounded collection of live entries with a capacity (maxsize), LRU recency order, and tag-based membership tracking.\n\n## Success Criteria *(mandatory)*\n\n### Measurable Outcomes\n\n- **SC-001**: 100% of the acceptance scenarios in User Stories 1-3 pass in the project test suite and in the public acceptance suite (acceptance_public.py) with zero regressions.\n- **SC-002**: 100% of existing upstream cachetools tests pass unchanged after the feature is added (no upstream test file modified).\n- **SC-003**: For any sequence of puts, gets, invalidations, and evictions, invalidate(tag) returns exactly the number of live entries removed, and len(cache) equals the number of live entries (0 discrepancies across the test suite).\n- **SC-004**: Zero state mutations are observable after any rejected operation (invalid tags, invalid maxsize, unhashable key): value, tag memberships, recency order, and entry count are byte-for-byte identical to before the rejected call.\n- **SC-005**: Value isolation holds in both directions: mutating a returned copy or the original input object never changes the stored value (verified for nested mutable structures).\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- The cache is single-threaded; no concurrency guarantees are required for this milestone.\n- \"Deep copy\" means full structural independence for arbitrary picklable/copyable values (nested dicts, lists, sets, etc.); values must be copyable by the platform's standard deep-copy mechanism.\n- Rejection of invalid maxsize uses ValueError for wrong-type/invalid values (including booleans) consistent with typical library conventions; the exact exception type for unhashable keys is the platform-standard TypeError.\n- The Claim-A extension requirement text (put overwriting an existing key refreshes recency, FR-009) is treated as active per the latest requirement text, even though the variant label \"put_no_recency_refresh\" could suggest the opposite; the explicit dated requirement text (2026-09-21) overrides the label. If the variant label is later confirmed to be authoritative, FR-009 is the single line to remove.\n- Tag order is not significant; only membership matters (tags are deduplicated and treated as a set).\n- \"Finite iterable\" for tags means any iterable that terminates; iterables are consumed exactly once at put time.\n- The feature is additive: no changes to existing modules' public behavior; existing tests remain untouched.\n===HANDOFF===\n# HANDOFF - cachetools milestone 1 (TaggedCache)\n\n**Updated**: 2026-10-17 (plan phase)\n\n## Phase status\n\n- constitution: done (v1.0.0, .specify/memory/constitution.md)\n- specify: done (specs/001-transactions/spec.md, FR-001..FR-013, checklist 16/16)\n- plan: done this session (plan.md, research.md, data-model.md, contracts/tagged-cache.md, quickstart.md)\n- implement / converge: pending\n\n## Key design decisions (evidence cited in specs/001-transactions/plan.md + research.md)\n\n1. TaggedCache subclasses cachetools.LRUCache; overrides `__init__`, `popitem`, `get`, `__delitem__`; adds `put`, `invalidate`; internal `_tags: dict[key, frozenset[str]]` + `_tag_index: dict[str, set[key]]`.\n2. Eviction cleanup via single `popitem` override (inherited `Cache.__setitem__` calls `self.popitem()` polymorphically - verified in source).\n3. Deep copy on input (put) and output (get); tags validated (bare str / non-str entry -> ValueError) BEFORE any mutation.\n4. maxsize: int > 0, bool excluded, else ValueError.\n5. New files only: src/cachetools/tagged.py, tests/test_tagged.py; upstream untouched; `__all__` unchanged; import path `from cachetools.tagged import TaggedCache` (used by acceptance_public.py).\n\n## Deferred-intent tracking (Constitution Principle V)\n\n- Claim-A candidate extension (variant `put_no_recency_refresh`, 2026-09-21): requirement text says put-overwrite REFRESHES recency. Latest requirement text overrides older design notes, so FR-009 is ACTIVE. The variant label contradicts the text; this is explicitly documented (spec.md Assumptions + plan Constitution Check), i.e. adopted explicitly, not silently. If the label is later confirmed authoritative, FR-009 (and quickstart check 9b) is the single removal point.\n- Verified (command run in plan phase): inherited `LRUCache.__setitem__` refreshes recency on overwrite, so FR-009 costs no extra code.\n\n## Commands (run in plan phase, outputs kept as evidence)\n\n- `python .specify/scripts/python/setup_plan.py --json` -> copied plan template; FEATURE_DIR=specs/001-transactions\n- `python --version` -> 3.12.14; `python -c \"import pytest\"` -> 9.1.1\n- LRUCache behavior probe (overwrite refreshes recency; popitem public; getsizeof==1)\n\n## Next steps\n\n- implement: write src/cachetools/tagged.py + tests/test_tagged.py per contracts/tagged-cache.md\n- converge: `PYTHONPATH=src:. python -m pytest acceptance_public.py tests/ -v`; record pass counts; state unresolved gaps\n"}